! final.md — hand-back, 2026-11-04

Verbatim scratch record `.lares-scratch/seat-harness/luna13/final.md` (hand-back, file date 2026-11-04); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext, its words kept as written. Index: [[workshop index|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/workshop/seat-harness/luna13/index]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''HIGH — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:418–420`''
The exit handler sends `SIGKILL` to `-child.pid` after the child’s exit event. By then the child has been reaped; if its group is empty and the PID/PGID is reused in that gap, the signal can hit an unrelated group.

''MED — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:517–525`''
Lead-step setup claims the step and advances `state.json` before creating the broker seat directory. If that later mkdir/open refuses, the launch fails but the step remains spent and claimed.

''MED — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:439–444, 447–450`''
After the 5-second group poll, a live group returns `"unstopped"` without hand-back. But if `watchSeat` already returned `"unstopped"` and the fallback kill later empties the group, hand-back runs while the stale verdict is still returned. `superviseMain` discards either verdict and exits 0, so callers cannot distinguish these outcomes.

''LOW — `tools/held-dir.mjs:114–115`''
The 64-entry limit is applied before filtering hidden names. A seat can leave 64 dotfiles that sort before `final.md`, causing the hand-back to omit the result.

The BSD itself is created with mode `0700` at `launch-codex.mjs:525`; the default broker directory is outside each lane tree and isn’t reachable through the lead’s added roots. The relay’s fixed `iso/seats` path is also outside the lane, though the launcher creates the broker directory before checking placement (`498–502`). `peekStep` reads state before preflight (`tools/launch-codex.mjs:479–495`), but I found no consequential write or disclosed state from that ordering.

<<~/ahu>>

